sentences.text:
10. Having considered the aforesaid facts and circumstances of the case and keeping in view the fact that undisputedly a marriage has taken place between the informant's daughter and the applicant;
that although the FIR alleges that the applicant has turned his wife out of her matrimonial home,
the victim had stated in her statement her father (the informant) had brought her back from her matrimonial home; that prima facie the FIR has been lodged because of some matrimonial dispute between the applicant and his wife and that the applicant is a young man having no criminal history and he is languishing in jail since 04.09.2024 whereas the investigation stands concluded, I am of the view that the aforesaid facts are sufficient for making out a case for enlargement of the applicant on bail in the aforesaid crime.

12. Let the applicant-Lal Bahadur Patel be released on bail in the aforementioned case on furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of Magistrate/Court concerned, subject to following conditions:-
(i) the applicant shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence;
(ii) the applicant shall not pressurize the prosecution witnesses;
(iii) the applicant shall appear on each and every date fixed by the trial Court.
.
[Subhash Vidyarthi, J.]

